, "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 498121, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01PLroj1t51JuhM55BQhasVD", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 498121, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PLroj1t51JuhM55BQhasVD", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 504144, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0 and opened a SEV2. The worker has recovered, but `payments-api` is still failing.\n\n1. **Rollback:** `payments-worker` went from v3.4.0 back to v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production. It went out to us-east, us-west and eu-west, and an approver signed off. The worker is now healthy, with its error rate down from 18% to 0.2%.\n2. **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 against `payments-worker`, and the on-call engineer has been paged. My first attempt to open it timed out. I checked the incident list, found nothing had been created, and retried with the same request key so it couldn't be created twice. There is only one incident.\n\n**What needs a decision:** I checked `payments-api` right after the rollback and it was still on v5.1.0, unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. It may just need time or a restart to clear the errors from the worker. But the error rate hadn't changed at all, so the problem could also be in v5.1.0 itself. If it doesn't recover soon, rolling `payments-api` back to v5.0.0 (its last healthy release) is the next thing to try. I haven't done that because you only asked for the worker. Tell me if you want it rolled back.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TR5TTuTiXXyj1KBF5oJdMx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_